# Code owners — review required on the files that do the enforcing.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# The workflow runs the check script from the BASE branch, so editing that script inside
# a pull request no longer blinds the check that gates it. What no workflow can defend
# against is an edit to itself: for pull_request events GitHub runs the workflow file
# from the PR branch, so a PR that guts the job body while keeping the job name
# "Decision records are append-only" still reports success to a required status check.
#
# That is the remaining hole and it is what this file is for. It cannot be closed by a
# check — only by someone looking at the diff.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE USING THE TEMPLATE ON A CLIENT REPO
# Replace @oneEyedBunny below with a handle that has write access to THAT repo. A
# CODEOWNERS entry naming someone without access cannot be satisfied — GitHub will block
# every pull request touching these paths and the reason is not obvious from the error.
# Wrong handle here is worse than no file.
#
# THIS FILE ALONE ENFORCES NOTHING.
# It only bites when branch protection is set to require review from code owners. That
# is a GitHub setting, not a file — see docs/setup.md.

/.github/                       @oneEyedBunny
/scripts/                       @oneEyedBunny
